rarpar-bench macOS port of par3cmdline 2971702e501f1350b1c7b9d11369af9157d6ed56.

BENCH-ONLY PATCH. It is applied by `rarpar-bench par3 build-reference` on
macOS hosts only, to the pinned upstream source archive, so the reference can
be compared against rarpar on Apple M-series machines. Linux and Windows build
the archive unmodified. The patch changes portability glue only: it routes
Darwin through the POSIX platform layer, uses the BSD stat timestamp names,
and keeps the x86-only SIMD compile flags and BLAKE3 sources off non-x86 CPUs
(BLAKE3 falls back to its portable C path). Leopard's ARM path additionally
needs sse2neon.h, which the harness fetches at a pinned commit and verifies.
No coding, matrix or file-format logic is touched.

